1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
In 2023, a federal judge sanctioned lawyers $5,000

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:16,220
for six court decisions invented by ChatGPT.
This is CiteWarden - the checking layer.

3
00:00:16,220 --> 00:00:22,520
Paste any text. Every citation is extracted and checked

4
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:31,020
against Crossref, OpenAlex, PubMed, the official eCFR -
and 464 verified landmark cases.

5
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:37,380
Score 97. Zero false accusations.

6
00:00:37,380 --> 00:00:44,980
The engine audits itself on labeled fixtures, on every page load:

7
00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:52,480
real citations must pass, fabrications must be caught.

8
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:57,300
100% - with the ground truth open-sourced.

9
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:06,500
Now the real case: Mata v. Avianca - six fabricated citations,
word for word from the court order.

10
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:18,000
Every fake goes red - watchlist, impossible volumes, era forensics.
The two real cites? Never accused.

11
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,680
Amber never guesses: it says, honestly, unverifiable.

12
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:32,980
Every green verdict carries its evidence:
the resolved title, the year, a link to the source.

13
00:01:32,980 --> 00:01:45,600
And the whole report is one shareable link -
paste it into your brief, your paper, or your filing.

14
00:01:45,600 --> 00:02:14,880
And this is not just for lawyers. Every verified case explains
itself in plain language. Paste a legal letter, and understand
what is actually being cited at you.

15
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:36,390
CiteWarden - because AI should cite, not invent.
